  comment   = {[Abstract-only record - publisher full text not held.] Introduces a practical four-grade MRI system for lumbar neural foraminal stenosis on sagittal MRI: grade 0 none; grade 1 mild (perineural fat obliteration in two opposing directions); grade 2 moderate (obliteration in four directions without morphologic change); grade 3 severe (nerve-root collapse or morphologic change). Evaluated on 576 foramina in 96 patients (L3-L4 to L5-S1) by two radiologists. Inter- and intra-observer agreement was near-perfect (kappa approx. 0.80-1.0). Direct clinical precursor to the left/right foraminal narrowing targets in the RSNA challenge.},
  note      = {},
}

