  comment   = {PRISMA systematic review and meta-analysis of traditional machine learning and deep learning for diagnosing lumbar spinal stenosis, drawing on PubMed, Embase and Cochrane. Twelve studies covering 15,044 patients were pooled (4 at high risk of bias, 3 unclear, 5 low). Pooled sensitivity was 0.84 (95\% CI 0.82-0.86) and specificity 0.87 (0.84-0.90), diagnostic odds ratio 36, SROC AUC 0.92 - both with very high heterogeneity (I2 approx. 99\%). The authors conclude that despite strong experimental numbers, no current model is reliable enough for real clinical practice, citing the need for accepted reference standards, multimodal strategies, larger datasets, external validation and fuller reporting. The best broad evidence map for AI grading of lumbar stenosis and its methodological weaknesses.},
