  comment   = {Early CAD method for automatically localising lumbar intervertebral discs in clinical MRI, combining HOG (Histogram of Oriented Gradients) features with an SVM classifier and hand-designed heuristics. Unlike prior work that returned only a point inside each disc, it outputs a tight bounding box per disc, letting a downstream CAD system skip a difficult segmentation step and work directly on the detected region. Achieves 99\% disc localisation accuracy on 53 clinical cases (318 lumbar discs), with purpose-built metrics for box accuracy and tightness. A historical precursor to anatomy-aware lumbar MRI pipelines.},
  note      = {},
}

